--
-- Out-of-database rasters: a raster band can name a file on the server
-- instead of holding its pixels.  A commit holds the raster's bytes, so
-- the path, band number and metadata come back byte-identical through
-- reset, checkout, merge and a file-remote clone, and the pixels are read
-- from the file wherever the raster is.  The file itself isn't versioned:
-- rewrite it, and every commit's raster reads the new pixels.
--
\set ECHO none
written|0
reads the file|1:true:6:78,2:true:6:78
band kinds|1:true/true,2:false/true
commit|t
branch|t
commit edit|t
reset back|t
reset: same bytes|t
reset: reads the file|1:true:6:78,2:true:6:78
reset forward|t
checkout|t
checkout: same bytes|t
checkout: reads the file|1:true:6:78,2:true:6:78
side commit|t
checkout main|t
merge|{0,0,"merge successful"}
merged: reads the file|1:true:6:78,2:true:6:78,3:true:6:78
remote|t
push|t
clone|t
clone: same bytes|t
clone: reads the file|1:true:6,2:true:6,3:true:6
rewritten|100
now|1:true:106:1278,2:true:106:1278,3:true:106:1278
reset to the first commit|t
its bytes|t
its pixels: the new file's|1:true:106:1278,2:true:106:1278
nothing to commit|0
